    "name": "european-beech",
    "notes": "A CROWN THAT DARKENS THE GROUND BENEATH IT, which is a PLACEMENT property as much as a shape one and is authored in both: the densest foliage of any broadleaf here (coverage 0.95 at separation 1.55, against the oak's 0.85 at 1.9) and a wide minimum spacing so a beech stand is beeches and nothing else.\n\n`distichous` habit -- leaves two-ranked into one flat plane held level to the light -- which is what makes a beech spray a spray and is the single most beech-like thing the generator can say. The smooth unfissured pewter bark cannot be said at all: bark texture is below the lattice, so what carries it is the very clean unbranched lower bole (`clear_frac` 0.45 with almost no wander).",
